 ],
 "synopsis": "KKR, Singtel, and Tata Communications have put their data centre company, STT GDC India, up for sale at a valuation exceeding $5.5 billion. The potential multi-billion transaction aims to rebalance capital requirements and streamline data centre plans. STT GDC India operates 34 data centres across 10 centres in the country with a total capacity of 613 MW. The shareholders initiated plans to sell their local operations to unlock value amid a global deals rush for data infrastructure capacity. Concurrently, the shareholders had also evaluated an Indian IPO for the business at a $6 to $7 billion valuation. KKR, STT GDC India, Singtel, and Tata Communications either declined to comment or did not respond to inquiries.",
